## Context

The original ticket called for a 45-run factorial. Rescoped to a
proof-of-concept: tool + unverified modes on the best extraction
(DeepSeek V3.2 decomposed, F1=98.8%, 167 plants).

During implementation, fixed verify_tool to use the LP reconciler
(was using a naive threshold-70 fuzzy matcher that produced 12 false
matches). Also fixed reconcile.py _extract_entries misclassifying
"Mismatched" LP status as EXACT_CAPACITY_DIFF.

LLM modes (self, cross) and web mode deferred to ticket 0048 —
OpenRouter too slow for 167-plant JSON verification prompts.

## Deliverables (PR #218)

1. `tabulate_verification.py` — sweeps evidence_score thresholds 1-4,
   evaluates each filtered subset via LP reconciler, outputs CSV + LaTeX
2. `derived/verification/tradeoff.csv` — precision/coverage/F1 per threshold
3. `report/inputs/generated/tab_verification.tex` — LaTeX table
4. Report Perspectives paragraph: empirical cost-of-trust result
5. Slides: "Cost of trust" frame in Verification section
6. Makefile targets for reproducible generation
7. `verify_tool` rewritten to use LP reconciler

## Key result

At threshold >= 3 (require one primary source):
- 163 plants retained (97.6%), 4 hallucinations rejected
- Precision = Coverage = F1 = 100%

## Exit criteria
- [x] Tool + unverified modes run, results in measurements.jsonl
- [x] `derived/verification/tradeoff.csv` with precision-coverage per threshold
- [x] One slide showing the cost-of-trust trade-off
- [x] One paragraph in report Perspectives
- [x] Full factorial commented in experiments.toml, split to ticket 0048
- [x] verify_tool uses LP reconciler (not naive fuzzy)
- [x] `make check-fast` passes (868 tests, 1 xfail)
